            "treatment.0",
            "treatment.1",
            "treatment.2",
            "treatment.3",
            "treatment.4",
            "treatment.5"
          ],
          "text": "On admission, blood glucose was 'HI' on BM (laboratory glucose 34), ketones 5.2, pH 7.18 and bicarbonate 11, consistent with severe DKA. PICU was informed and she was managed on ward HDU. She was treated with cautious IV fluids, fixed-rate insulin infusion, potassium replacement and hourly monitoring per DKA protocol. By day 2 (18/05), pH had improved to 7.34 and ketones to 0.8. She was transitioned to subcutaneous insulin on a basal-bolus regimen. The diabetes nurse and dietician provided input, and structured education covering carbohydrate counting, hypo management and sick-day rules was delivered. Both parents and child were confident with injections and monitoring prior to discharge.",
